title: DummyIntro
---
Dummy: Heya!
Dummy: You can hit me as much as you want... I don't mind!
Jamie: I'll take that as a challenge!
===
title: SurfaceArrival
---
Jamie: My god… we made it, Dinky. We really made it.
Dinky: Nyeh!
Jamie: Look at it all! This is what we’ve been living under all this time? It’s… amazing!
<<legacy_dialogue_event>>
Jamie: Do you think Uncle got to see it? He must have, right?
<<legacy_dialogue_event>>
Dinky: Nyeh nyeh!
<<legacy_dialogue_event>>
Jamie: We’re gonna find him, Dinky. We’re gonna find him and get you back to normal. That’s what we came here for, right?
<<legacy_dialogue_event>>
Dinky: Nyeh…
<<legacy_dialogue_event>>
Jamie: Wait… Dinky, do you see that? Over there, by the lake. What is—Gasp! The town! No!
<<legacy_dialogue_event>>
Jamie: There has to be something left. Come on, Dinky, we gotta see!
<<legacy_dialogue_event>>
===
title: Journal1
---
Uncle: Dear Jamie,
Uncle: If you’re not Jamie– buzz off, mate.
Uncle: But god, kid, I hope it’s you. If I’m right, you’re the one reading this letter, with that goofball of yours— Dinky, was his name? Sorry, the exhaustion is getting to me.
Uncle: I feel like I’m losing my memories.  But I don't want to. 
Uncle: So I’m hoping you’ll find these letters and bring them back to me someday.
Uncle: There seems to be only one real path going up, so unless you’re lost, kid, you’ll run into my other letters too. I’m gonna write them every so often, all the way to the top.
Uncle: Hold on, I gotta go. I can hear something. Love you, kid! 
Jamie: Oh my god. Oh my god! You know what this means, Dinky? Uncle took this same route! He’s still out there, and he’s waiting for us!
Dinky: Karuumph!
Jamie: Of course I’m gonna ask him about his journey when I see him! Let’s keep moving, munchkin! 
===
title: Journal2
---
Jamie: Dinky! Its another one of Uncle's journals!
Uncle: Dear Jamie,
Uncle: Dude, if you’re not Jamie, then seriously, stop reading. 
Uncle: Bad news, Jamie. I dropped the music box somewhere along my journey. I must have put it down somewhere. I’m so sorry, kid. I hope you find it.
Uncle: I used to play its music when I was having rough one down here. Or when I missed home.
Uncle: I think about the day I left a lot. Y’know, your dad and I had a huge argument that day. We almost came to blows.
Uncle: Your dad has always looked up to me, but this day... something broke between us. Does he still talk about me?  
Uncle: And you! You were so sad that I left, and to be honest, so was I, kid. But I knew I had to leave.
Uncle: The waste creature attacks were getting out of hand, and I knew the only way to solve the problem was to get to its root.
Uncle: Everybody thought I was crazy for deciding to face the Waste head on. They wouldn’t support me. Did you know even your parents thought I was insane? 
Uncle: But I don’t regret my decision. I’m going to reach the surface and I will find a way to help the people of New Lutum.
Dinky: Karuumph!
Jamie: Yeah! Let's return the music box to Uncle when we see him!
===
title: Journal3
---
Uncle: Hi kid,  I’m writing this with a broken wrist, so my handwriting may be worse than usual. Don’t laugh at it, I know it’s bad, eh?
Uncle: Also, don’t fret, kid, the wrist is healing already. Thanks to these creatures nearby. I hope you’ve befriended them already, they are truly godsends.
Uncle: My hand’s already begun hurting, but I’m sure you’re doing better than I have been. And I hope Dinky’s been helping you out a little bit, that menace. I didn’t realise how fond of him I was either.
Uncle: Your parents have always trusted the little guy, but I only began understanding these little creatures’ minds after this journey.
Uncle: Nothing is ever as valuable as what the road teaches you. I’m sure you’ll realise that in good time. Which better be soon, because I think we’re both nearing the end.
Uncle: I have to go now, it looks like the animals are struggling with something. It’s only fair to help them out too, yeah? One good for another. See you on the upper side, kid.
Jamie: He was helping them. Of course!
Dinky: Spoooekksshh!!
Jamie: And he said he’s nearing the end! Yahoo! Let’s get going, Dinky!
