===
title: BirthdayIntro
---
The clock strikes twelve and a young girl rushes downstairs with her pet in tow. Her parents follow after her, carrying a birthday cake.
She doesn’t pause, quickly blowing on the candles and distractedly cutting the cake before running into the living room, where a pile of presents awaits her on the coffee table.
Dominic Quila: Jamie! Good lord! At least take Dinky with you, or I’m going to trip over him!
Dinky: Neeeyhhh!
Alex Quila: Honey, at least blow out all your candles!
Digging through the pile, Jamie hunts for a specific gift, Dinky at her heels. She pulls out a present wrapped in red and white striped paper. 
The tag reads "Happy birthday, Jamie. I'm always thinking of you. Love, Uncle." Jamie rips the package open to find a purple gas canister.
Jamie: I knew it!
She runs over to the sofa and reaches far underneath it, pulling a harpoon gun out.
She lifts the gas canister and fits it into its spot.
It’s finally done!
She begins to aim outside the window.
Her parents appear behind her and snatch the gun out of her hands. 
Dominic Quila: Don’t point that in the house! What do you think you're doing Jamie? God, it's your fifteenth birthday, and you're still building toys? And that too, behind our backs?
Alex Quila: How long has the stupid thing been under the sofa?
Jamie: Hehe, as long as you haven't vacuumed under there, Papa.
Alex Quila: Jamie. I'm being serious.
Jamie: For a few months now. No one else knows about it.
Jamie: Well, maybe if you'd been more supportive of my dream I might have told you earlier!
Dominic Quila: Hold on, supposedly no one knows, yet Uncle knew exactly which part to give you, precisely when you needed it?! God, Jamie.
Jamie: It's not like I could have told him, Mama. He somehow still knows me better than anyone here.
Alex Quila: Knew you. Your uncle is long gone, sweetheart, and you should come to terms with it.
Alex Quila: Besides, no one has ever gone beyond the Underground, and neither should you. It's too dangerous, and you know that. You need to start focusing your time elsewhere now, honey.
Jamie: Uncle went.
Alex Quila: Look how that turned out. He’ll likely be the first and last. 
Jamie: I am brave like him, Papa. I've never wanted to do anything else, and you know that! I want to explore the world, not rot away in some corner of darkness.
Dominic Quila: This is not "some darkness", Jamie, this is our home! And you're going to have to adjust your expectations, because you are never, ever going up to the surface! 
Jamie purses her lips, her eyes filled with rage.
Jamie: We'll see about that. Let's go, Dinky-boy.
She grabs the harpoon gun back from her mother and sprints outside with Dinky before they can catch her.
Dominic Quila: It's too late for excursions, young lady!! Come back, now!!!
Alex Quila: She'll cool off and be back, sweetheart. Besides, all she's doing is firing that prototype. Plus, Dinky's with her.
Dominic Quila: That silly creature is going to be the death of me.
===
title: City2CrazyOldMan
---
Crazy Old Man: What’s eatin’ ya, squirt?
Jamie: Dinky touched the Waste…
Crazy Old Man: Doggonit! He’s a goner, he is! ‘Less you get ‘im up there, ‘course.
Jamie: Up… there? You mean, the surface?
Crazy Old Man: Yeah! The sun oughta do ‘im some good.
Jamie: (Going back? I wonder if Uncle made it up there… if he did, maybe he could help. This might be the only way.)
Jamie: Well Dinky, looks like the only way to go is up. You ready, boy?
===
title: City2Doctor
---
Jamie: Doctor, please, I need your help! It’s Dinky, I found him covered in Waste in the Underground.
Doctor: It appears the Waste has mutated him… Forgive me, Jamie, I know how important Dinky is to you, but I cannot help you. Our resources are limited, so I have to save them for the people of this town.
Jamie: That’s… such a dumb excuse! 
Jamie: Why… why can’t you help him? He’s my best friend, Doctor.
Doctor: The Waste is dangerous, Jamie. We mustn’t mess with it.
Jamie: Maybe someone else can help Dinky.
===
title: City2Marshall
---
Marshall Kane: Is that… Dinky?
Jamie: Yes! I found him!
Jamie: But I think the Waste changed him. Please, can you help?
Marshall Kane: If Dinky has become a Waste creature… I owe it no mercy. Hand it over… it will be a swift end.
Jamie: NO! I won’t give you Dinky!
Jamie: I need to find someone else who can help. 
===
title: CityConstructionWorker
---
Construction Worker: God, it’s ridiculous how we’re trying to “grow” New Lutum.
Construction Worker: No one new’s moving in, and obviously the Waste creatures aren’t happy with us intruding on their territory. Only a guard would be brave enough to open the gate right now.
===
title: CityDoctor
---
Doctor: Jamie, hello. That was quite a loud sound from the outskirts, I pray you were not harmed?
Jamie: Doctor, it’s good to see you! No, no, I’m fine.
Doctor: Excellent, I am quite pleased to see you uninjured for once. Did you have another reason for seeking me out?
Jamie: Yeah, it’s about Dinky. He was scared off by that sound and he ran out into the Underground! Could you help me open the gates? Please! I need to find him!
Doctor: My apologies, Jamie, but I’m unable to leave my clinic. What would transpire if someone were to arrive, injured, and I’m not here to attend to them post haste?
Doctor: Perhaps someone more suited to combat could assist you? 
Jamie: Thanks, Doctor…
===
title: CityGuard
---
Guard: Careful, kid. We’ve been seeing a rise of aggressive Waste creatures around New Lutum lately. I wonder why… 
Jamie: Oh no! My pet Dinky ran out of the town a few minutes ago! Please, would you be able to help me open the gate? It’ll just be for a moment, I promise I’ll find him and come back quick!
Guard: Hm, I did just say it’s getting more dangerous in the Underground, but I lost a pet once. The grief never leaves you.
Guard: C’mon, I’ll help you open the gate, just don’t tell anyone, okay?
Jamie: Oh, thank you! Thank you so much!
===
title: CityMarshall
---
Marshall Kane: Jamie. That loud sound… is your harpoon gun working?
Jamie: Marshall Kane! Yes! Well, kind of? It seems to be working but I didn’t think it would be that loud.
Marshall Kane: Hm, keep up your training. With your skills… you could join me one day… to protect this town from the Waste monsters.
Jamie: Actually, that’s what I came here for.  Dinky got into the Underground, but I can’t get out to help him! Would you be able to help me open the gate?
Marshall Kane: What?
Jamie: It’s Dinky! He got scared when we were training and he burrowed past the gate. I need to get him back!
Marshall Kane: I can’t help. The dangers past the gate… if they were to make it in here… sorry, Jamie. The other guard… she also lost a pet… 
